B.adA=new A.aS(u.O,u.x,"Frontiers in Human Neuroscience, 12, 353",2018,"https://doi.org/10.3389/fnhum.2018.00353","Slow breathing techniques (especially at ~6 breaths/min) consistently increase parasympathetic activity, improve HRV, and enhance EEG alpha-band power - markers of relaxed alertness.")
B.ae9=new A.aS("Cardiac Vagal Tone, Plasma TNF, and Sustained Attention in Healthy Adults","Thayer, J. F. & Fischer, J. E.","Brain, Behavior, and Immunity, 23(4), 510-513",2009,"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.bbi.2009.01.002","Higher resting HRV (achievable through breathing practices) predicted better sustained attention performance, linking vagal tone directly to morning cognitive readiness.")
B.aeq=new A.aS("The Effect of Diaphragmatic Breathing on Attention, Negative Affect and Stress","Ma, X., Yue, Z. Q., Gong, Z. Q. et al.","Frontiers in Psychology, 8, 874",2017,"https://doi.org/10.3389/fpsyg.2017.00874","Eight weeks of diaphragmatic breathing practice significantly reduced cortisol levels, decreased negative affect, and improved sustained attention compared to controls.")
