B.LE=new A.b6("breathe","\ud83c\udf2c\ufe0f","5 min slow breathing at ~6 breaths/min","Slow breathing at 6 breaths/min reliably increases parasympathetic activity","Zaccaro et al., Front Hum Neurosci, 2018","https://doi.org/10.3389/fnhum.2018.00353",B.a0a,"Three slow breaths, sitting exactly where you are.")
B.adH=new A.aS("Adapted Cold Shower as a Potential Treatment for Depression","Shevchuk, N. A.","Medical Hypotheses, 70(5), 995-1001",2008,u.bc,"Cold exposure activates the sympathetic nervous system and increases norepinephrine by 200-300%. Proposed mechanism for antidepressant effects via dense cold receptor activation in skin.")
B.ae_=new A.aS("The Effect of Cold Showering on Health and Work: A Randomized Controlled Trial","Buijze, G. A., Sierevelt, I. N., van der Heijden, B. C. et al.","PLOS ONE, 11(9), e0161749",2016,"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0161749","In a large RCT (n=3,018), routine cold showers resulted in a 29% reduction in sickness absence from work. Participants reported increased energy levels and quality of life.")
B.ae8=new A.aS("Human Physiological Responses to Immersion into Water of Different Temperatures","Sr\xe1mek, P., Simeckov\xe1, M., Jansk\xfd, L., Savl\xedkov\xe1, J., & Vyb\xedral, S.","European Journal of Applied Physiology, 81(5), 436-442",2000,"https://doi.org/10.1007/s004210050065","Cold water immersion at 14\xb0C increased norepinephrine by 530% and dopamine by 250%. Even milder cold exposure (20\xb0C) produced significant catecholamine increases within minutes.")
