B.aa4=new A.fD(["Walker, M. P.","Sleep occurs in 90-minute cycles - waking between cycles feels refreshing, waking mid-cycle causes grogginess.","Sleep occurs in 90-minute ultradian cycles containing light sleep (N1\u2013N2), deep sleep (N3), and REM. Waking between cycles feels refreshing; waking mid-cycle causes sleep inertia.","\ud83c\udf19","Scribner","Why We Sleep: Unlocking the Power of Sleep and Dreams","https://doi.org/10.1126/science.aax5843",2017])
B.aa0=new A.fD(["Irish, L. A., Kline, C. E., Gunn, H. E., Buysse, D. J., & Hall, M. H.","A consistent 30\u201360 minute wind-down routine reduces time to fall asleep by 37%.","A consistent 30\u201360 minute pre-sleep wind-down routine reduced sleep onset latency by 37% in adults with mild insomnia, establishing behavioral cues that signal the brain to prepare for rest.","\ud83d\udd6f\ufe0f","Sleep Medicine Reviews, 22, 23-36","The Role of Sleep Hygiene in Promoting Public Health","https://doi.org/10.1016/j.smrv.2014.10.001",2015])
B.aa7=new A.fD([u.Z,"Caffeine has a 5\u20136 hour half-life - a 3 PM coffee still has 50% active caffeine at 9 PM.","Even when caffeine doesn't prevent falling asleep, it reduces deep sleep (N3) by 15\u201320%, meaning you sleep longer but recover less. A 10-hour cutoff eliminates 75% of the dose before bedtime.","\u2615",u.ce,u.g,"https://doi.org/10.5664/jcsm.3170",2013])
B.aa8=new A.fD(["Winter, B.","The Military Sleep Method helped 96% of fighter pilots fall asleep in 2 minutes after 6 weeks of practice.","The Military Sleep Method was developed for fighter pilots to fall asleep in 2 minutes under any conditions. Progressive muscle relaxation and cognitive clearing are the core techniques.","\ud83e\uddd8","A.S. Barnes & Company","Relax and Win: Championship Performance in Whatever You Do","https://doi.org/10.1016/j.smrv.2002.01.002",1981])
B.aa3=new A.fD([u.i,"Writing a to-do list before bed helps you fall asleep 9 minutes faster than journaling about completed tasks.","Participants who wrote a specific to-do list for the next day fell asleep significantly faster than those who journaled about completed tasks - offloading unfinished business reduces pre-sleep cognitive load.","\ud83d\udcd3",u.cS,u.M,"https://doi.org/10.1037/xge0000374",2018])
B.aa_=new A.fD([u.s,"Evening bright light delays melatonin onset by 30\u201390 minutes, shifting your internal clock later.","The suprachiasmatic nucleus uses light as its primary zeitgeber. Evening bright light (>100 lux) delays melatonin onset by 30\u201390 minutes. Intensity matters more than color temperature.","\ud83d\udd04",u.aF,u.p,"https://doi.org/10.1210/jc.2010-2098",2011])
B.aa1=new A.fD([u.bu,"A cool room (65\u201368\xb0F / 18\u201320\xb0C) accelerates sleep onset by helping your core temperature drop.","Core body temperature must drop 1\u20131.5\xb0C to initiate sleep. Warming the skin (warm bath, socks) paradoxically cools the core by dilating peripheral blood vessels, speeding sleep onset.","\ud83c\udf21\ufe0f","Journal of Applied Physiology, 87(4), 1489-1495","Role of Body Temperature in Sleep Regulation","https://doi.org/10.1152/jappl.1999.87.4.1489",1999])
B.a9X=new A.fD(["Lally, P., van Jaarsveld, C. H. M., Potts, H. W. W., & Wardle, J.","Habit formation takes an average of 66 days - and missing two consecutive days significantly increases dropout.","Habit formation takes an average of 66 days, not 21. Consistency matters more than intensity, and missing one day doesn't reset progress - but missing two consecutive days significantly increases dropout risk.","\u2b50","European Journal of Social Psychology, 40(6), 998-1009","How Are Habits Formed: Modelling Habit Formation in the Real World","https://doi.org/10.1002/ejsp.674",2010])
B.Yw=s([B.aa4,B.aa0,B.aa7,B.aa8,B.aa3,B.aa_,B.aa1,B.a9X],t.aM)
B.aah=new A.HX("SLEEP SCIENCE",B.Yw,null)
B.aaa=new A.fD(["M\xf6ller-Levet, C. S., Archer, S. N., Bucca, G. et al.","Sleep deprivation for just 24 hours changes the expression of over 700 genes.","One week of insufficient sleep altered the expression of 711 genes, including those involved in circadian rhythms, sleep homeostasis, oxidative stress, and metabolism.","\ud83e\uddec","Proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences, 110(12), E1132-E1141","Effects of Insufficient Sleep on Circadian Rhythmicity and Expression Amplitude of the Human Blood Transcriptome","https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1217154110",2013])
B.aa2=new A.fD(["Raichle, M. E. & Gusnard, D. A.","Your brain uses 20% of your total energy despite being only 2% of body weight.","The brain consumes 20% of total body oxygen and glucose despite comprising only 2% of body weight, reflecting its extraordinarily high metabolic demands.","\ud83e\udde0","Proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences, 99(16), 10237-10239","Appraising the Brain's Energy Budget","https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.172399499",2002])
B.aab=new A.fD(["Duffy, J. F. & Czeisler, C. A.","Morning sunlight exposure can advance your circadian clock by up to 2 hours.","Morning light exposure phase-advances the circadian clock by up to 2 hours, while evening light delays it. Timing is the critical variable for circadian entrainment.","\u2600\ufe0f","Sleep Medicine Clinics, 4(2), 165-177","Effect of Light on Human Circadian Physiology","https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jsmc.2009.01.004",2009])
B.a9Z=new A.fD([u.R,"Even 1-2% dehydration impairs cognitive performance measurably.","Even mild dehydration (1-2% body water loss) impairs cognitive performance, mood, and concentration. Regular hydration throughout the day is essential for sustained brain function.","\ud83d\udca7","Nutrition Reviews, 68(8), 439-458","Water, Hydration and Health",u.N,2010])
B.aa5=new A.fD(["Szuhany, K. L., Bugatti, M., & Otto, M. W.","Just 20 minutes of walking increases BDNF, promoting brain cell growth.","A single bout of exercise increases peripheral BDNF levels. Regular exercise amplifies this effect, promoting neurogenesis and synaptic plasticity in the hippocampus.","\ud83c\udfc3","Journal of Psychiatric Research, 60, 56-64","Exercise and the Brain-Derived Neurotrophic Factor","https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jpsychires.2014.10.003",2015])
B.aa6=new A.fD(["Xie, L., Kang, H., Xu, Q. et al.","The brain clears toxic waste proteins (including beta-amyloid) during deep sleep.","The glymphatic system clears neurotoxic waste products (including amyloid-beta) from the brain during sleep, with clearance rates increasing 60% compared to wakefulness.","\ud83d\ude34","Science, 342(6156), 373-377","Sleep Drives Metabolite Clearance from the Adult Brain","https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1241224",2013])
B.a9Y=new A.fD(["Yano, J. M., Yu, K., Donaldson, G. P. et al.","The gut produces ~95% of the body's serotonin - diet directly affects mood.","Gut microbiota regulate serotonin biosynthesis in the colon, with indigenous spore-forming bacteria promoting serotonin production. Diet-driven microbiome changes directly alter serotonin levels.","\ud83e\udd57","Cell, 161(2), 264-276","Indigenous Bacteria from the Gut Microbiota Regulate Host Serotonin Biosynthesis","https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2015.02.047",2015])
B.aa9=new A.fD([u.bj,"4 days of brief meditation training improves working memory and executive function.","Just 4 days of brief mindfulness training significantly improved visuospatial processing, working memory capacity, and executive functioning compared to active controls.","\ud83e\uddd8",u.l,u.L,u.bH,2010])
